course: dictionary
lesson: 2899
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «Sugar is bad,» says Dad, eating a doughnut, «but grown-ups need energy.» Dad is eating it, so a doughnut here is the sweet cake.
explain: Now read «a ring doughnut». The word can also mean any ring shape, like a ring cushion or a rubber ring. Ask yourself: what is the thing like? If it is round with a hole in the middle, the second meaning fits.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «eating a ring cushion» make sense? No, so the first meaning is right in that sentence. Does «a rubber ring» fit the second meaning? Yes, it does.
fact: A doughnut is a small sweet cake of fried dough, often shaped like a ring with a hole.
fact: Some doughnuts are round balls filled with jam or cream, like a jam doughnut.
fact: Any ring shape can be called a doughnut, such as a ring cushion or a rubber ring.
fact: Doughnut is also spelled donut, especially in the USA.
fact: «Timbits» are little doughnut balls from Tim Hortons.
exercise: «Bram goes red, then buys her a box of Timbits, little doughnut balls from Tim Hortons.» What are Timbits? | Sweets made of sugar only | *Little doughnut balls | Boxes for keeping toys | Small red birds
exercise: 12 doughnuts are shared equally by 4 children. How many does each child get? | *3 | 48 | 4 | 8
exercise: Which of these is a doughnut in its second meaning, a ring shape? | A square biscuit | A sheet of paper | *A rubber ring | A long, thin stick
test: «Nobody lied about anything; Alfie just took the trouble, and his friend bought him a doughnut.» What did Alfie's friend buy him? | A bus ticket | A new bike | A cup of tea | *A doughnut
test: Which spelling of doughnut is used especially in the USA? | *Donut | Doughnutt | Dounut | Dohnut
exam: Which phrase shows doughnut in its first meaning, a sweet cake? | A rubber ring | A ring doughnut | *A jam doughnut | A ring cushion
